    <worksheet name='Placement vs. Luck'>
      <layout-options>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>A player beats her expected goals for two reasons. Placement (horizontal) is the goals-worth of where she put the ball, from ASA&apos;s xplace field. The diagonal is where the whole margin is placement; distance above it is everything placement does not explain - keeper errors, deflections, posts. 34 players with a finishing margin of at least 1.5 goals either way, out of 134 qualifying. Non-penalty, 2026 season to date. Data: American Soccer Analysis.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='nwsl_2026_placement' name='federated.07f5mtl09llim61fe0hn91v2dy1z' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.07f5mtl09llim61fe0hn91v2dy1z'>
            <column caption='Material' datatype='boolean' name='[Calculation_1904807382077441]' role='dimension' type='nominal'>
              <calculation class='tableau' formula='ABS([Margin]) &gt;= 1.5' />
            </column>
            <column caption='Diagonal' datatype='real' name='[Calculation_1904807384334338]' role='measure' type='quantitative'>
              <calculation class='tableau' formula='SUM([Placement])' />
            </column>
            <column datatype='real' name='[Goals]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column datatype='real' name='[Margin]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column datatype='real' name='[Placement]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column datatype='string' name='[Player]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
